# Copy to .env (git ignores it) and set what you need. `frun` reads .env from the
# directory you run it in, and from the directory your agent file lives in.
# Anything exported in your shell wins over this file.
#
# These are the settings people actually change. Everything else — limits, token
# lifetime, a keys file, turn detector plugins — has a working default and is in
# the README.

# ---- Secrets ----
# Hugging Face, for gated or private models (frun models pull hf:...)
# HF_TOKEN=hf_...
# Only when the LLM is a hosted endpoint that needs a key
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# ---- Authentication ----
# The keys this server accepts (frun key new). Without any, it answers on
# localhost only, and `frun up --host 0.0.0.0` refuses to start.
# FUSION_ACCEPTED_KEYS=web:frun_...
# Websites whose pages may open a socket. Unset: only pages this server serves.
# FUSION_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://shopkart.example
# Your TLS-terminating proxy, if there is one (RunPod, nginx, Cloudflare).
# Until it is named here, its X-Forwarded-* headers are ignored.
# FUSION_TRUSTED_PROXY=10.0.0.0/8
# The key this machine presents when talking to a server somewhere else. For a
# server on this machine, `frun talk` and `frun token` use the key above.
# FUSION_API_KEY=frun_...

# ---- What to run ----
# An agent file: prompt, models, turn settings (same as `frun up agent.py`)
# FUSION_AGENT=./agent.py
# Used when there is no agent file: development | production | hybrid
# FUSION_CONFIG=development
# Where models are downloaded to and loaded from
# FUSION_MODEL_DIR=./models

# ---- Turn taking ----
# Silence before the agent answers, in milliseconds
# FUSION_TURN_WAIT_MS=500
# How long the caller must talk over the agent before it stops
# FUSION_INTERRUPT_AFTER_MS=300

# ---- LLM from an OpenAI-compatible endpoint (vLLM, llama-server, Ollama) ----
# All three go together; the key is named, never written here
# FUSION_LLM_URL=http://localhost:8080/v1
# FUSION_LLM_MODEL=my-model
# FUSION_LLM_API_KEY_ENV=OPENAI_API_KEY

# ---- Logs ----
# pretty (a terminal) | json (deployments and log collectors) | off
# FUSION_LOG_FORMAT=pretty
# Write transcripts and replies into the logs (off by default)
# FUSION_LOG_CONTENT=0
